  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WN WASH response to South Sudanese refugees in Elwaral camp</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Interventions in this programme document are designed to respond to the humanitarian hygiene needs in this new camp. Activities include Participatory Hygiene Sanitation Transformation (PHAST); Raise awareness on personal, environmental and household hygiene through daily home visits, radio and Interpersonal communication, community dialogue, drama/theater performances, hand washing promotion, water point support /household and jerry can cleaning demonstrations; Conduct hygiene promotion message dissemination and campaigns, follow up the hygiene promotion work alongside community leaders and the hygiene promoters on daily basis; celebrating with Open Defecation Free in Eldibaba village to encourage the community to keep using the latrines and represent a good method which other surrounding communities can follow.</narrative>
  </description>
